Package: skatR
Title: Analysis and Simulation of the Card Game Skat
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Raban", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: A toolkit for the German card game Skat. Provides a configurable
    rules engine supporting both official tournament rules and common casual
    variants, bidding value computation, players ranging from rule-based
    heuristics through determinized Monte Carlo search to an exact
    double-dummy solver, Monte Carlo simulation over many deals, and tidy
    analysis and visualisation of outcomes. Card play, scoring and game-value
    calculation follow the standard 32-card Skat deck.
